The fresh false-postcondition mutation is discriminating: it parses/builds successfully, but changing the increasing example’s required result from `"ccc"` to `"bb"` yields `WarnStuckClaimState` and exit 1 with the actual final output still `"ccc"`. The static inventory found no concrete false rule; the remaining issue is narrower—a missing universal K theorem connecting the proof-only `seqVal` representation to the concrete `listVal` representation.
